<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Camp Windy</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:190-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.310224" lon="-121.641836"><ele>1426.3</ele><name>Bennett Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 367401558 'Bennet Pass Sno-Park'); Forest Road 3550 passes 6 m from it; as in 189-2; confidence: high; pdf_page: 188; book_elev_ft: 4674; quote: The trail starts at Bennett Pass Sno-Park and goes 2.4 miles to the Terrible Traverse along a splendid, rolling, forested ridge following a primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.298990" lon="-121.608880"><ele>1463.9</ele><name>Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse)</name><desc>source: OSM node 5164478227 on Forest Road 3550, the DEM low point (4,803 ft); as in 189-2; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 189; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: the trail descends to Windy Saddle at the west foot of the Terrible Traverse</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.279104" lon="-121.596418"><ele>1632.9</ele><name>Bonney Junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 3669713797 (Gunsight Trailhead) on Forest Road 3550, where Gunsight Trail #685 (the road north) and Forest Road 4891 leave it; DEM 5,357 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 191; book_elev_ft: 5360; quote: At Bonney Junction (5,360 feet), a forested saddle, roads lead to Camp Windy and Bonney Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286393" lon="-121.588045"><ele>1712.6</ele><name>Windy Point</name><desc>source: OSM node 3669738830 on Gunsight Trail #685, 0.69 mi from Bonney Junction and 0.26 mi before Camp Windy, on the climb to the DEM crest (5,646 ft at 0.79 mi); placed past map 41's 5520' dot (DEM 5,520 ft at 0.53 mi, matching the map's 0.5) and by the text's 0.4 mi scaled to the OSM road (map legs 1.2 vs OSM 0.95); confidence: low; pdf_page: 192; quote: ski north through forest on a scenic route to Windy Point, a shoulder with unusual rock formations, and good views to the north and east. This breezy shoulder, often windpacked, is the logical end of the tour as Camp Windy just 0.4 mile farther has little more to offer</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.289979" lon="-121.586767"><ele>1704.5</ele><name>Camp Windy</name><desc>source: OSM node 3667973324, where Camp Windy Trail #685B (the road northeast to Badger Lake) leaves Gunsight Trail #685 (the road north along Gunsight Ridge); 0.95 mi along the road and 0.89 mi straight NNE of Bonney Junction; DEM 5,592 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 192; quote: Camp Windy is located 1 mile northeast of Bonney Junction at the head of Boulder Creek ... From Camp Windy one road leads north along Gunsight Ridge and Lookout Mountain, and one leads northeast to Badger Butte, Badger Lake, and Grasshopper Point</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Camp Windy</name><desc>1. Bennett Pass Sno-Park -&gt; Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse): osm (high), 2.24 mi | 2. Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse) -&gt; Bonney Junction: osm (high), 1.78 mi | 3. Bonney Junction -&gt; Windy Point: osm (high), 0.69 mi | 4. Windy Point -&gt; Camp Windy: osm (high), 0.26 mi</desc>
